# Forever and retail. Classic Era's 11509 is deliberately absent: the Era
# compatibility in the code stays, because it costs nothing and is what makes
# the differences on the other two legible, but nothing is shipped for it.
#
# Retail earned its place rather than being assumed into it. Both clients are
# on the 12.0 codebase, so they share the parts that were expensive to get
# right - secret values, restricted aspects, the taint rules. An audit of
# every Blizzard name BazUI references against what each client actually
# loads found nothing present on one and missing from the other:
# tools/client-diff-audit.py, which is also where Blizzard's load model is
# written down.
#
# What that audit cannot see is behaviour, and that is where the real
# differences will be. A name existing is not the same as it doing the same
# thing.
## Interface: 16001, 120100
# A readable copy of the line above. The client does not expose
# "Interface" through GetAddOnMetadata, but it does expose any X- field,
# so this is how /baz sv can say whether the TOC it is running was the
# one on disk - a TOC is only re-read when the client launches, never on
# /reload, and a test that cannot tell those apart proves nothing.
## X-Interface-Stamp: 16001,120100
## Title: BazUI
## Notes: One addon for your whole interface: bags, action bars, unit frames, nameplates, chat, minimap and a notification center, sharing one look and one settings panel.
## Author: Baz4k
## Version: 011
## X-License: GPL-2.0-or-later
## X-Copyright: Copyright (C) 2026 Baz Studios LLC
## X-Website: https://github.com/BazAddons/BazUI
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1698481
## Category: BazUI
## X-Category: Interface Enhancements
## SavedVariables: BazUIDB
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: BazUICharDB
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Gizmo_GoblingTonkController

# 16001 is World of Warcraft: Forever 1.60.1; 11509 is Classic Era, where
# development started. Those are the two clients this addon runs on, and
# nothing else belongs here.
#
# Tried and abandoned: leading with 120100 (retail Midnight) because one
# addon that appeared to save its settings declared it first. It made no
# difference - measured with the stamp below, on a cold start, with the
# settings seed cleared so nothing could mask it - and the addon it was
# based on turned out not to save reliably either. The saved variables bug
# is the client's, it affects everyone, and no TOC line works around it.
# See Core/Seed.lua. Declaring retail support we do not have would only have
# put the addon in front of players it was never built for.
#
# /baz sv prints what the client asks for against this, and whether the
# per-character file remembers more than one load.

# Before everything: stands in for the saved variables the client will not
# read. Empty in the repository; tools/bake-seed.py fills in a local copy.
# Must stay first, because an addon file runs before its saved variables do
# and the real ones are meant to overwrite this.
Core\Seed.lua

