# Chat, back on for testing (2026-09-18).
#
# It was off because a chat replacement has to assign DEFAULT_CHAT_FRAME,
# and assigning a global Blizzard reads taints every call that reads it -
# which was believed to break Edit Mode. Re-checked against the client's
# own source since: that read is in EditModeManager's
# NotifyChatOfLayoutChange, reached on a spec change or when a layout is
# applied, not on opening Edit Mode. BazUI also has its own Edit Mode now,
# and UnitColor no longer lets a secret colour reach a widget.
#
# So the blocker is narrower than it was written up as, and worth
# measuring rather than assuming. If it does misbehave, the fix is to stop
# assigning that global at all: make window 1 be ChatFrame1, restyled,
# rather than a frame of ours that has to claim its name.
#
# To switch off again, comment the block below back out.
Modules\Chat\Core\Init.lua
Modules\Chat\Core\Frames.lua
